-      see both the outer border color and the inner border color(s) adjacent to it.
-      It then picked the most frequent adjacent mapped color, which depends on local
-      perimeter counts and is not a nesting-aware rule.
-    - variant logic instead assigns each enclosed bg component to the smallest adjacent
-      sprite bounding box that strictly contains the whole component. This makes the
-      outer annulus belong to the large sprite, while an inner hole belongs to the
-      smaller sprite inside it.
-    - difference: ownership is now based on containment hierarchy rather than raw
