-"""
-Design analysis for the D11 nested-sprite variant
-
-spec_variant:
-  preserved_core:
-    - bg is still the dominant border color and is still 0 in generated tasks
-    - a 2xN or Nx2 palette still sits on exactly one grid edge
-    - the palette still maps border colors to fill colors
-    - hollow monochrome sprites are still the only objects that can trigger fills
-  d11_change:
-    - instead of several isolated sprites, each scene contains one large hollow sprite
-      whose interior cavity contains one or more smaller hollow sprites
-    - at least one inner sprite is also palette-keyed, so the outer cavity is adjacent
-      to multiple candidate border colors at once
-    - the output must fill the large outer cavity while leaving inner sprite borders
-      untouched, and then fill any inner holes owned by palette-keyed inner sprites
-  concrete_pixel_behavior:
-    - input: border-only scene. The large ring and the inner ring(s) are all hollow.
-    - output: the annulus between outer ring and inner ring(s) is filled with the
-      outer ring's mapped fill color; each fillable inner ring also has its own hole
-      filled with its mapped color; distractor inner rings remain hollow.
-  behavior_trace:
-    - original logic on a nested annulus would inspect one enclosed bg component and
-      see both the outer border color and the inner border color(s) adjacent to it.
-      It then picked the most frequent adjacent mapped color, which depends on local
-      perimeter counts and is not a nesting-aware rule.
-    - variant logic instead assigns each enclosed bg component to the smallest adjacent
-      sprite bounding box that strictly contains the whole component. This makes the
-      outer annulus belong to the large sprite, while an inner hole belongs to the
-      smaller sprite inside it.
-    - difference: ownership is now based on containment hierarchy rather than raw
-      adjacency frequency.
-  complexity_calibration:
-    - at least one enclosed region is intentionally adjacent to >=2 mapped border
-      colors, so nesting is visually and algorithmically active in every sample
-    - inner sprites remain rectangular rings to keep the containment cue readable
-      from only a few examples
-    - palette size is kept small (2-4) and colors are all distinct across border,
-      fill, and distractor roles to avoid hidden color collisions
-  implicit_assumption_audit_for_main:
-    - _best_palette still assumes the palette is isolated on the edge; generator keeps
